doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22115109"
message: "If you use citeguard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "citeguard: retraction, correction, and expression-of-concern checking for citations"
abstract: >-
  citeguard checks whether a cited work has been retracted, corrected, or
  flagged with an expression of concern, by querying the Crossref REST API.
  It reads both publisher-asserted update records and the Retraction Watch
  records Crossref backfills, because many retractions -- including the 1998
  Wakefield MMR paper -- carry no structured retraction metadata from the
  publisher at all and are only visible through the latter. It ships as a
  Python library and command-line tool, a Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  server for AI agents, and a GitHub Action for continuous integration, all
  sharing one detection implementation.
